##POST ON YOUR PAGE AND SUBMIT ANALYTICS 
Once your clips are edited and ready, the next step is to publish them on your social media page and submit the required analytics to the campaign.
The objective is to generate views, meet campaign requirements and get your performance verified for payment.


Publish clips on your social media page - 
Open your designated social media account (Instagram, TikTok or YouTube).
Upload the edited clip.
Write an engaging caption relevant to the video.
Add relevant hashtags if required.
Follow the campaign's tagging, mention and description requirements.
Publish the video.
Copy and save the published video URL.
Repeat the process for your remaining clips.


Important - 
Follow the campaign's posting frequency requirements.
Use a public account if the campaign requires public visibility.
Don't delete or archive published clips before the campaign's specified period.
Avoid misleading captions and artificial engagement.
Follow the campaign's rules regarding multiple accounts and platforms.


Track video performance - 
Views: Total video views
Likes: Number of likes
Comments: Audience interactions
Shares:  Number of times shared
Saves:  Number of times saved
Watch time:  Total time viewers watched
Engagement: Audience interaction with content


Submit analytics to the campaign - 
Open the campaign's submission channel or dashboard.
Find the analytics submission form.
Enter your social media username.
Paste the published video URL.
Provide the requested analytics.
Upload screenshots of the platform insights if required.
Submit your entry.
Keep a record of your submission for future reference.


Maintain a performance tracker - 
just a simple motion sheet with basic deatils like 
Clip    Platform   Views   Submission
Clip 01 Instagram  100     Pending
Clip 02 Instagram  10000   Pending
Clip 03 YouTube    200     Pending


Understand campaign payment - 
CPM: Payment per 1,000 eligible views.
Fixed payment: A predetermined amount for completing specified deliverables.
Performance-based: Payment based on views or other campaign-defined targets.
